<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26162" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lēgātārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		legatum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>enjoined by a last will</i> or <i>testament</i> (postclass.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">editiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Spect. 6</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lēgātārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>one to whom
				something is left by will, a legatee</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Galb. 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 41, 3, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gai.
				Inst. 2, 195</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antequam legatarius admittat legatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 200</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lēgātārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a female
				legatee</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 19, 11, 43</span></i>; <i><span class="en">33, 4, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
